pokeplatinum-widepointers.patch (tools/pokeplat_gen.py applies it to build/pokeplatinum, after the others): the pointer
pass's first rules, what Platinum's boot to the intro needed on a 64-bit host (docs/platinum.md, "Jobs, in order", 5.):
- every cast of a pointer to u32 or s32 clang reports (-Wpointer-to-int-cast, -Wvoid-pointer-to-int-cast) as a uintptr_t
  or intptr_t cast, made at the column clang gives (173 casts, 43 files; as pokebw2-pointers.patch did for Black 2).
  Never worse than before (a result stored in a u32 is cut as it was), right wherever the address is computed on and
  cast back. Not done: 6 inside macros (battle/healthbox.c's VRAM_TRANSFER_DST, game_overlay.c's DTCM bounds)
- savedata.c: the save blocks' addresses (bodyAddress, startAddress, footerAddress) as uintptr_t: SaveData_LoadCheck read
  the footers through a cut address (the first crash of the boot)
- heap.c: every heap twice its DS size where a pointer is 8 bytes (HEAP_HOST_SIZE: the system's from the arena, each
  child heap from its parent), as Black's WORK_AREA_SIZE and pokebw2-workareas.patch
